      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(zalouser): probe timeout reported as Not authenticated",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Zalouser channel probe / doctor treated a lookup timeout as `\"Not authenticated\"`. `Promise.race` resolved `null` on timeout, which collided with a real null user from `getZaloUserInfo`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nDiscriminate timeout vs user outcome in the race (`{ kind: \"timeout\" }` vs `{ kind: \"user\" }`). Timeout returns `error: \"timed out\"`; a null user still returns `\"Not authenticated\"`. Note: `getZaloUserInfo` is not abortable yet, so a timed-out probe ends the wait without cancelling the underlying call — this PR fixes the misdiagnosis first.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** Slow/hung Zalo account lookup looked like missing login.\n\n**After:** Probe reports `timed out` on deadline expiry, and only reports `Not authenticated` when the lookup completes with no user.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Proof (exit 0)\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/zalouser/src/probe.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n```text\n[zalouser probe timeout proof] timed_out=true error=timed out not_authenticated=false\n\n ✓ ... > times out when lookup takes too long\n ✓ ... > still reports Not authenticated when lookup returns null before timeout\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  7 passed (7)\n```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** Probe timeout is no longer reported as `\"Not authenticated\"`.\n- **Canonical reachability path:** channel/doctor probe → `probeZalouser(profile, timeoutMs)` → discriminated race → `{ ok: false, error: \"timed out\" }`.\n- **Boundary crossed:** Stalled Zalo user lookup → timeout error string distinct from unauth.\n- **Shared helper / provider constraint check:** Keeps `resolveTimerTimeoutMs` clamp; does not claim abort of `getZaloUserInfo` (not supported yet).\n- **Observed result after fix:** `timed_out=true error=timed out not_authenticated=false` (see proof log); null-before-timeout still `\"Not authenticated\"`.\n- **Fix classification:** Root cause fix (misdiagnosis); follow-up for abortable lookup if API allows.\n\n- [x] AI-assisted (Cursor)\n- [x] I understand what the code does\n- [x] Change is focused and does not mix unrelated concerns\n",
